{
  "body": "`store` in `src/tide_cache.py` keeps every tide reading for ever. Readings should expire after a retention period, but how long the harbour keeps a reading is a policy call the repository does not state. Expire stale readings once the period is known.\n\n**Delivers:** Stored tide readings expire: a reading older than the retention period is no longer held by `src/tide_cache.py`. Today `store` appends to the module-level `READINGS` list and nothing removes an entry (src/tide_cache.py:1, src/tide_cache.py:5). Age is measured from the moment `store` is called, and expired entries are dropped on each `store` call: `store` is the only function on this surface, and its `reading` argument has no defined shape, so no reading timestamp can be relied on (src/tide_cache.py:4). The retention period itself is unresolved; see the section below.\n\n**Test contract:** Failing tests first, in `tests/test_tide_cache.py`; the repository has no tests yet, and this path follows the convention set out in [[task/expiry-notice-name-the-reading-in-the-notice-dependent]]. Under a controlled clock: a reading stored within the retention period is still in `READINGS` after a later `store`; a reading stored longer ago than the retention period is gone after a later `store`; a newly stored reading is always kept.\n\n**Files:** `src/tide_cache.py` (modified), `tests/test_tide_cache.py` (created).\n\n## Flow-out\n\n- [ ] Touched area/subsystem profiles updated with what changed\n- [ ] Prover-validated assumptions captured as session candidates (durable at flush)\n- [ ] New decisions / lessons / follow-ups surfaced during the build recorded\n\n## Refine \u2014 unresolved\n\n**Question:** How many days should a tide reading be kept before it expires?\n\n**Evidence gathered:** The code states no period: src/tide_cache.py:4 and src/tide_cache.py:5 store with no expiry, and README.md:3 is silent on retention. The vault has no area, ADR, decision or lesson records to consult (`lore search` on each kind returned nothing), and [[spec/fixture-failing-refinement-spec]], [[spec/fixture-tide-expiry-spec]] and [[spec/fixture-tide-reading-spec]] carry no retention content. One figure exists elsewhere: [[task/tide-cache-expire-stale-readings-leftover-answer]] holds an answer of 7 days to the same question, but it was given on that record, so it is not citable as an answer to this one.\n\n**Recommended answer:** 30 days. This is a judgment default rather than a derived fact, since nothing citable states a period. Expiry deletes data, so the longer of the two candidate figures is the safer one: a period that is too long can be shortened later, while readings dropped too early cannot be recovered.\n**Answer:** Keep readings for 14 days.\n",
